 me from out  of 500 subscribers to 32,000 within  about a month and a half and then I  posted another video on how I make  rental income like passive income and  that got me from 32 to 50 thousand  subscribers and that was enough to  really get my initial wave on YouTube  and then at that point I was like holy  crap like now I'm actually making money  by doing this with the ad revenue and  now I see the potential and and so I  just continue doing that and and now  that income  it's just skyrockets it's almost you  know a hundred times to when I was  making back then it's just insane on  your first video correct me if I'm wrong  but it was you were talking about how  you became a millionaire at 26 and what  did you do you taught people how to be a  millionaire at like a young age that  video was more so just telling my story  okay there was nothing to sell in that  video is literally just this is what I  did mm-hmm  and these are some of the things that  you can learn from my experiences doing  that um but basically that video summed  up is that I saved everything I made  mm-hmm working as a real estate agent I  was the cheapest person alive I saved up  money for about three and a half four  years invested in real estate in 2011  fixed up those properties rented them  out those properties went up in value I  continued saving all the money I made as  a real estate agent continued investing  and then I'm sure after about seven  years of doing that I had a million  dollar net worth and that was just  before I turned 26 and you made all this  money from commissions on selling houses  so I got involved as a real estate agent  initially leasing property so I would  find because because that would to me at  the time was a really underserved market  was leasing so I would lease people  their houses I'd maybe make a thousand  bucks maybe two thousand dollars by  doing this no other agent wanted to  waste their time doing leasing because  why would they make a thousand dollar